// Phase M3 item 3 regression (--no-check LOWERER backstop): an undefined INSTANCE method `x.nope()` must
// not silently emit a bare `nope` external symbol even when the type-check pass is skipped. The M3 checker
// rejects it before lowering, but a `--no-check` build would otherwise reach codegen with methodCallee's
// UFCS fallback returning the bare selector `nope` (undefined -> dyld crash / garbage). requireResolved-
// MethodCallee hard-aborts in the lowerer when the resolved callee is a bare selector that is neither a
// defined free function nor an intrinsic. The gate compiles with `--no-check` and asserts abort + no binary.
struct Widget(val id: Int)

fun main(): Int {
  val w = Widget(1)
  return w.nope()
}
